  "body": "## What happens\n\n`import_model` accepts a Solidcraft design saved as `.sc` (#1456) but refuses the same design saved as `.solidcraft`: `import_model: unsupported file type: p01-flange.solidcraft`. Both are the same zip container (`document.json`, `container.json`, `cache/model.json`, `cache/bodies.bin`; the `.solidcraft` copy also carries `cache/thumbnail.*`), and SolidCraft keeps the `.solidcraft` name for a design opened with that extension. Workaround: save it again as `.sc`.\n\n## Expected\n\n`.solidcraft` imports exactly like `.sc` (MCP `import_model`, the GUI's open dialog filter, and drag-and-drop), and the thumbnail entries are ignored.\n\n## Repro (upstream main abe24ff09)\n\n`import_model {path: \"p01-flange.solidcraft\"}` -> refused; `import_model {path: \"p01-flange.sc\"}` (same design) -> 3124 facets, note \"Solidcraft design 'p01-flange': the cached final body only\".\n\nFound by the QA swarm (SolidCraft v0.44.1 + CamCraft v0.23.0, part p01-flange).\n\n**Done means:** a `.solidcraft` file imports the cached final body like a `.sc`, in MCP and the GUI; a test pins it.\n",
